#: includes/class-imgpro-cdn-media.php:938
msgid "Bandwidth Saver copies an image to your img.pro App the first time a page shows it, and from then on pages load it from img.pro. Images no page shows are not copied, and use none of your App's images, until you copy them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-imgpro-cdn-media.php:940
msgid "Serve images is off on the Bandwidth Saver settings page, so pages load every image from its original address and ask for no new copies. Copy to img.pro still works."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-imgpro-cdn-media.php:942
msgid "The img.pro column in list view, and the img.pro line in an image's details, show where each image is:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-imgpro-cdn-media.php:944
msgid "<strong>Copied</strong> means your App has a copy of the image. While Serve images is on, pages load it from img.pro, and sizes not copied yet are copied when a page shows them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-imgpro-cdn-media.php:945
msgid "<strong>Queued</strong> means the image is waiting to be copied. It loads from your server until then."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-imgpro-cdn-media.php:946
msgid "<strong>Not copied yet</strong> means your App has no copy of the image yet. While Serve images is on, it is copied the first time a page shows it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-imgpro-cdn-media.php:947
msgid "<strong>Copy failed</strong> means img.pro did not take the image. The reason is shown under the status."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-imgpro-cdn-media.php:948
msgid "<strong>Stays on your server</strong> means img.pro does not accept the file (for example because of its format or size), the file WordPress recorded is missing from the uploads folder, or img.pro blocked it. The reason is shown under the status."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-imgpro-cdn-media.php:949
msgid "<strong>Not an image</strong> means a document, video, audio or other file. These always load from your server."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-imgpro-cdn-media.php:950
msgid "<strong>Files not found</strong> means WordPress has no file recorded for the image in the uploads folder, so Bandwidth Saver cannot copy it. The image loads from its original address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-imgpro-cdn-media.php:952
msgid "<strong>Copy to img.pro</strong> copies every size of an image now instead of waiting for a page. Each size counts as one image in your App. To copy several images, select them in list view and choose Copy to img.pro from Bulk actions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-imgpro-cdn-media.php:953
msgid "Bandwidth Saver changes images in post content, widgets, featured images and images output with wp_get_attachment_image(). For an image whose URL a theme or plugin reads directly, such as theme CSS or a social sharing image, copy it and use <strong>Copy img.pro URL</strong> in its details."
msgstr ""

